  "description_html": "Skeletal diagram of <i>Soroavisaurus australis</i> showing known fossil material of the holotype (PVL-4690) and an two assigned specimens (PVL-4048 and PVL-4033), with unknown elements shown in gray and inferred from <i>Mirarce eatoni</i>.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"PVL-4690_and_PVL-4048\">PVL-4690 and PVL-4048</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Chiappe, Luis (1993). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270821578\">Enantiornithine (Aves) tarsometatarsi from the Cretaceous Lecho Formation of northwestern Argentina</a>\". <i>American Museum novitates</i> (3083): 1–27.</cite></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"PVL-4033\">PVL-4033</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\" id=\"Reference-Chiappe-2002\">Chiappe, Luis M. (2002) \"11. Skeletal Morphology and Systematics of the Cretaceous Euenantiornithes (Ornithothoraces: Enantiornithes)\" in Chiappe, Luis M., ed. (in English)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.co.uk/books/about/Mesozoic_Birds.html?id=GMQkDQAAQBAJ&amp;source=kp_book_description&amp;redir_esc=y\">Mesozoic Birds: Above the Heads of Dinosaurs</a></i>, University of California Press, pp. 240–267  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-520-20094-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-520-20094-4\">978-0-520-20094-4</a>. </small></cite></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"PVL-4048_and_PVL-4033\">PVL-4048 and PVL-4033</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\"> (2009). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.ria.ie/RIA/files/40/40a4c454-eef2-4de0-922d-48ae0c42037f.pdf\">Euenantiornithine birds from the Late Cretaceous of El Brete (Argentina)</a>\". <i>Irish Journal of Earth Sciences</i> <b>27</b>: 15–62. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.3318/IJES.2010.27.15\">10.3318/IJES.2010.27.15</a>.</cite></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Unknown_parts_inferred_from_Mirarce\">Unknown parts inferred from <i>Mirarce</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(<span class=\"mw-formatted-date\" title=\"2018-11-13\">2018-11-13</span>). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6238772\">The most complete enantiornithine from North America and a phylogenetic analysis of the Avisauridae</a>\". <i>PeerJ</i> <b>6</b>: e5910. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.5910\">10.7717/peerj.5910</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMID</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/30479894\">30479894</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed_Central\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed Central\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMC</span></a></span>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6238772\">6238772</a>.</cite></li></ul>",
